Package: com.hoshinoxxx.biloginalfx7
Name: BiloginalfX7
Version: 16.1-Alpha16.1
Section: Tweaks
Maintainer: HoshinoXXX
Author: HoshinoXXX
Architecture: iphoneos-arm
Depends: mobilesubstrate | cydia-substrate, firmware (>= 7.0)
Conflicts: com.jjr.bilifix7, com.hoshinoxxx.biloginalfx7probe, com.hoshinoxxx.biloginalfx7.bisect, com.hoshinoxxx.biloginalfx7.bisect2
Replaces: com.jjr.bilifix7
Tag: purpose::extension, compatible_min::ios7.0
Description: Revive the discontinued bilibili iOS client on iOS 7 and later.
 The app only talks to long-dead endpoints, so most pages and the player stopped working.
 This tweak registers an NSURLProtocol - the same layer as the app's own BiliURLProtocol,
 but matched first - and routes every legacy request to a current bilibili.com endpoint,
 rewriting the response back into the shape the old client expects. The app's own model
 and view code are left untouched. Four NSURLConnection entry points are hooked as a
 fallback for traffic that bypasses the URL loading system.
 .
 Why that layer: static analysis of the client binary shows the network stack is
 .
     business APIs -> BiliApiV2/V3 -> APURLConnectionOperation, a forked AFNetworking
                   -> -[NSURLConnection initWithRequest:delegate:]
                   -> BiliURLProtocol, an NSURLProtocol subclass the app registers
 .
 so the app already runs at the NSURLProtocol layer, and inserting there covers
 everything with a single hook point.
 .
 Covered endpoints:
  * Video detail and playback URL, with WBI signing and automatic avid/cid injection
  * Comments, danmaku and replies
  * Home feed and regions - primary regions via the UWP channel, secondary regions
    emulated by keyword search because the original service has been shut down
  * Search for all, bangumi, movie and uploader, with per-endpoint User-Agent handling
  * Bangumi index, detail and ranking
  * 32-bit ID overflow fix: avid, cid and mid virtualization with persistent maps
  * Risk-control handling: full browser fingerprint, buvid3 plus buvid4, anonymous
    endpoints, request throttling
  * Login state injection, by rewriting the nav response so the old client realises
    it is signed in
 .
 No runtime dependencies - nothing but MobileSubstrate is required. The same package
 works on both iPhone and iPad.
 .
 This package exists only so that a discontinued client can keep reaching public content.
